    <!-- ========================================================= IOS DIGITS -->
    <!-- Plain document artboard (no state machine, no view model): the R9 percentage
         digits as STROKE SKELETONS and the inline charging bolt. The ten skeletons are
         generated offline from IosDigits.kt (cap 60.7, stroke 12.1, equal advance 64.3)
         and authored as open/closed PointsPaths under a round-cap/round-join Stroke.
         There is no Fill: the runtime draws these centre lines with Paint.Style.STROKE,
         so the terminals are semicircles and the ink width is skeleton + stroke = the
         IosDigits glyph width (50.8/26.7/43.0/44.0/49.2/44.0/46.1/42.5/45.7/46.8).
         Arc/cubic segments are flattened at 5 deg / 16 segments, the only RML-
         expressive conversion; stroke width, cap, joins and advance are exact.
         The inline bolt sample is the 40 x 59 knockout shape; RML has no PorterDuff
         CLEAR, so the sample is a filled patch with the bolt marked as a hole; the runtime
         clears the same outline inside the battery fill. -->
